2. Architectural Origins: How Platforms Source Menu Data

Understanding how each platform procures and stores menu records determines the structure, completeness, and reliability of the data retrieved:
Platform	Primary Function	Menu Source of Truth	Data Format & Quality
Tabit	POS (Point of Sale) & ERP	Direct merchant entry into the Tabit Cloud POS system. Real-time kitchen & stock synchronization.	Highly structured relational JSON (modifiers, kitchen groups, taxation, variants).
Ontopo	Table Reservation & Seating	Manual restaurant upload via merchant console. Often treated as secondary to table availability.	Mixed; mostly static assets (PDFs, images stored on S3/CloudFront) or flat text.
Wolt	Food Delivery & Marketplace	Merchant portal entry with strict catalog validation by Wolt operations.	Clean, highly standardized normalized relational JSON schema.
10bis	Corporate / Retail Delivery	Merchant portal / POS integrations with localized categorization.	Hierarchical JSON tree (categories -> dishes -> dish options).
